__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
# Stored rollouts and run metadata. Trajectories are the expensive artifact and MUST be
# persisted (CLAUDE.md 4), but a 6,600-episode sweep is ~28MB and belongs in object
# storage rather than in git history.
#
# The small results files the gates are checked against ARE committed, and not only for
# the record: test_gate_a_thresholds_preregistered and test_gate_b_thresholds_preregistered
# compare the gate config's commit timestamp against the results file's, and an UNTRACKED
# results file makes that check return early and pass without comparing anything. A gate
# whose enforcement is silently skipped is a note. (Re-including a file needs the parent
# directory un-ignored first -- git will not descend into an excluded directory.)
runs/*
!runs/phase0/
runs/phase0/*
!runs/phase0/results.json
!runs/phase3/
runs/phase3/*
!runs/phase3/prompted_baseline.json
data/synthea_output/
*.jsonl.gz
.DS_Store


# SLURM job logs. One file per job id, and a GRPO run writes 2000 step lines plus vLLM's
# startup output -- committing them would pollute the repo and conflict on every pull.
# The directory itself IS tracked (via .gitkeep) because SLURM refuses to launch a job
# whose --output directory does not exist.
slurm/logs/*
!slurm/logs/.gitkeep
